# Phase 10 lineup/event blobs — large generated data, minified by the sync
# writer (writeJsonStableMin). Prettier must NOT reformat them: it would inflate
# the committed size ~2x AND break the cron's idempotent diff (sync writes
# minified, prettier rewrites pretty → noise PR every run).
data/lineups-*.json
data/events-*.json

# Cross-season search index — written by writeJsonStable (each array element on
# its own line), but prettier inlines short arrays (e.g. "aliases": ["laca"]).
# That format drift breaks the cron's idempotent diff (sync rewrites multi-line
# → noise PR every run) and used to require a manual `git checkout` after every
# commit. writeJsonStable owns this file's formatting; prettier must not touch it.
data/search-index.json

# TASK-1606 Arabic-name sidecar maps — written by the build/apply scripts via
# writeJsonStable (sorted keys). Prettier must not reformat them (keep the cron's
# idempotent diff stable).
data/i18n/names-ar/*.json

# SDP history side-map — written by the one-off build-official-stats-history.ts
# via writeJsonStable (recursively sorted keys). writeJsonStable owns its
# formatting; prettier must not touch it, so a builder re-run + commit can never
# produce a prettier-vs-writer diff (matches the search-index/names-ar policy).
data/player-history-stats.json

# TASK-M68 market-value side-maps — written by apply-market-values.ts via
# writeJsonStableMin (sorted keys, minified). The writer owns their formatting;
# prettier must not touch them, or a re-apply produces a prettier-vs-writer diff
# on every run AND re-inflates them ~1.5x (same policy as search-index.json /
# player-history-stats.json / lineups-*.json above).
data/market-value*.json
